  "method": "Anguilla and its offshore cays (Dog Island, Scrub, Prickly Pear, Sandy Island, Sombrero); Sombrero, 60 km out, appears only on the national-trust park list and is excluded. Anguilla publishes no official dive-site or mooring list: the Anguilla National Trust page names the six marine parks (Dog Island, Prickly Pear, Little Bay, Shoal Bay-Island Harbour, Sandy Island, Sombrero) but no dive sites, so it is cited and not counted for names. The lists weighed are the Anguilla Tourist Board's dive pages (anguilla-vacation.com and ivisitanguilla.com, one body, counted once), Scuba Shack's own site list (its news page and the full 15-reef, 7-wreck list its package page carries, hosted by Carimar Beach Club; Shoal Bay Scuba and Scuba Shack are the same business), and Open Seas Charters' scuba page. Anguillian Divers' domain is gone and Special D's site is a blog with no site list, so neither could be counted; no other operator publishes a list. A site is counted when it is on at least two of these three. Sandy Island is treated as the umbrella for Scuba Shack's three Sandy dives. El Buen Consejo is excluded as a closed or limited-access heritage wreck. Counted 2026-10-14.",
